// The streams package: the shapes a transform of bytes takes, written once with
// no I/O inside, so that inflate, deflate, zstd and a hash run in any stage of
// a pipeline: over a file, a socket, an actor's mailbox or a buffer in memory.
// It holds layer 1 of Cone's streaming design (a codec core) and layer 2, a
// Reader and a Writer for the stage that holds the bytes (reader.cone and
// writer.cone). Stages between actors, layer 3, are package stages': they need
// the actors runtime, which these layers (and the codecs that import them) do
